{"text": "SBA 7(a) LOAN APPLICATION -- BORROWER INFORMATION SUMMARY\nPrepared by Whitlock-Tan & Associates, CPAs for submission to First Bitterroot Bank\nLender contact: Marcus Delgado, VP Commercial Lending, mdelgado@firstbitterroot.example, 406-555-0170\nDate prepared: 08/31/2026                      Lender ref: FBB-SBA-26-00419\n\nA. APPLICANT BUSINESS\nLegal name:      Tamarack Ridge Brewing Co., LLC  (d/b/a \"Tamarack Ridge\")\nEIN:             81-4092275\nAddress:         1180 Railyard Spur, Unit C, Missoula, MT 59802\nFormed:          March 11, 2019 (Montana LLC, taxed as a partnership -- files Form 1065)\nEmployees:       14 (9 full-time)\nWeb:             www.tamarackridgebrewing.example\n\nB. LOAN REQUEST\nAmount:          $640,000, 10-year term\nUse of proceeds: 10-barrel brewhouse expansion ($410,000); refinance equipment note with\n                 Northern Rockies Equipment Finance, Inc., loan no. NRE-0077-31854, payoff $148,220.16;\n                 working capital ($81,779.84).\n\nC. OWNERS (20% or more) -- from SBA Form 1919 and Form 413\n1. HAUGEN, INGRID SOLVEIG -- 60%, managing member\n   DOB Nov. 8, 1984   SSN 115-14-4666   MT driver's license 0811198441208\n   Home: 742 Cherry Blossom Court, Missoula, MT 59801. Cell (406) 555-0124.\n   U.S. citizen: yes. Criminal history question: YES -- misdemeanor DUI, 2011, disclosed.\n   Personal net worth per Form 413: $386,400.\n2. Babajide Akinwande (\"Jide\") -- 40%, head brewer\n   DOB 1990-02-17   SSN 168964978\n   Home: PO Box 317, Lolo, MT 59847. Cell 406.555.0186. jide@tamarackridgebrewing.example\n   U.S. citizen: no -- lawful permanent resident, card no. A-208-661-573.\n   Personal net worth per Form 413: $71,950. Student loans of $38K outstanding.\n\nD. BANKING\nOperating account: First Bitterroot Bank, routing 102296990, account 2000417738\nPayroll account:   Clark Fork Federal Credit Union, routing 124493946, account 77-104-5529\nAverage collected balance, last 12 months: $58,300\n\nE. COLLATERAL OFFERED\n - Brewhouse and fermentation tanks (to be purchased); existing glycol chiller, serial GC-2291-0457A\n - 2021 Ford Transit delivery van, VIN 1FTFW1E53NC506833, MT plate 4-71802B\n - Second lien on Ms. Haugen's residence (first mortgage balance $214,000)\n\nF. FINANCIAL HIGHLIGHTS (from the reviewed statements)\n                       FY2024        FY2025        YTD (7 mos.)\n Revenue             1,412,880     1,688,415       1,104,270\n Net income             61,340        97,125          72,060\n Owner draws            84,000        96,000          56,000\nDebt service coverage on the proposed loan: 1.41x on 2025 results.\n\nG. PREPARER'S NOTES (not for the lender package)\nIngrid wants the taproom lease assigned before closing; landlord has not answered.\nJide's green card expires next June -- lender will ask; he has the renewal receipt.\nThe 2025 owner draws include twelve thousand dollars that went to Ingrid's brother and should be\nreclassified as a loan. FWT to discuss before we sign the compilation letter.\n\nFlorence Whitlock-Tan, CPA (MT license PAC-CPAP-LIC-004417)\nflorence@whitlocktancpa.example   office 406 555 0111", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "394 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Ingrid Solveig Haugen", "Babajide Akinwande", "Ingrid", "Jide", "Florence Whitlock-Tan"], "companies": ["Whitlock-Tan & Associates", "First Bitterroot Bank", "Northern Rockies Equipment Finance, Inc.", "Tamarack Ridge Brewing Co., LLC", "Montana LLC", "Clark Fork Federal Credit Union", "Idaho Falls National Bank", "Ford", "FWT"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Missoula", "Montana", "Lolo", "example"], "health": [], "sensitive": ["criminal history question"], "names": ["Ingrid Solveig", "Babajide", "Jide", "Ingrid", "Florence Whitlock-Tan"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999925494194, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 23793.10000000149, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_